 ## Security Considerations
 - **Payment Fraud**: Validate LNURL responses and Bitcoin TXIDs; implement rate-limiting (e.g., 10 requests/minute) to prevent abuse.
 - **Price Manipulation**: Display `price` verbatim; enforce payment.
 - **Private Key Security**: Use [nsecBunker](https://nsecbunker.com/) or NIP-07 (e.g., [Nos2x](https://github.com/fiatjaf/nos2x)) for key management.
 - **Media Privacy**: Use [nostr.build](https://nostr.build/) for metadata removal.
 - **Access Control**: Encrypt paywalled `file` URLs and sensitive metadata (e.g., `license` terms) per [NIP-04](https://github.com/nostr-protocol/nips/blob/master/04.md).

 ---

 ## Backwards Compatibility
 - Unknown `kind: 1001` events display as text notes (`content` field) per [NIP-01](https://github.com/nostr-protocol/nips/blob/master/01.md).
 - Clients ignoring `price`, `lightning`, or `bitcoin` tags treat content as free, ensuring seamless integration with existing Nostr clients.
 - Compatible with [NIP-01](https://github.com/nostr-protocol/nips/blob/master/01.md) and [NIP-21](https://github.com/nostr-protocol/nips/blob/master/21.md).

